THIRD-PARTY DATA NOTICES

Some files in this repository contain numbers taken from, or computed from, data
published by others. They are listed one by one, with the source address and the
terms that were read, in data/README.md. The Apache License applies to the
EconSim code and to EconSim's own work; it does not change the terms of the
original data. Attribution:

- U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA): International Energy Statistics and
  Short-Term Energy Outlook (October 2026), https://www.eia.gov/. Source: U.S.
  Energy Information Administration.
- U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis (BEA): international transactions, international
  investment position, direct investment, NIPA tables. Source: U.S. Bureau of
  Economic Analysis.
- U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics (BLS): unemployment rate. Source: U.S. Bureau of
  Labor Statistics.
- U.S. Census Bureau: foreign trade statistics. Source: U.S. Census Bureau.
- Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System: H.15 selected interest rates,
  H.10 foreign exchange rates and trade weights. Source: Board of Governors of the
  Federal Reserve System.
- U.S. Department of the Treasury: Treasury International Capital (TIC) system,
  including the Survey of Foreign Portfolio Holdings (SHL, SHC).
- Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis, FRED(R): series retrieved from FRED. This
  product is not endorsed or certified by the Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis.
- Freddie Mac, Primary Mortgage Market Survey(R) (30-year fixed-rate mortgage
  average, retrieved from FRED as MORTGAGE30US): 24 monthly values in
  scripts/data/us_now.json. Source: Freddie Mac. See "Items to confirm" in
  data/README.md.
- World Bank, World Development Indicators (NY.GDP.MKTP.CD, NY.GDP.MKTP.PP.CD):
  licensed under CC BY 4.0. Used to compute GDP weights; changes were made.
- International Monetary Fund (IMF): World Economic Outlook data used to fill gaps
  in GDP weights and as reference growth rates (DataMapper NGDP_RPCH); parameter
  values from IMF Working Paper WP/13/87 (Carabenciov and others, "GPM6: The
  Global Projection Model with 6 Regions"). Source: IMF. See "Items to confirm" in
  data/README.md.
- OECD, Balanced International Merchandise Trade Statistics (BIMTS) and Trade in
  Value Added (TiVA, 2025 edition): used to compute bloc trade weights; changes were made. See
  "Items to confirm" in data/README.md.
- Bank for International Settlements (BIS), locational banking statistics. Source:
  BIS.
- European Central Bank (ECB), "The international role of the euro" (June 2026
  edition, Table 1). Source: ECB.
- The Budget Lab at Yale, "The State of U.S. Tariffs" (editions of 8 April and 24
  August 2026), https://budgetlab.yale.edu/. See "Items to confirm" in
  data/README.md.
- Peterson Institute for International Economics (PIIE), Chad P. Bown, "US-China
  Trade War Tariffs: An Up-to-Date Chart" (22 August 2026). See "Items to confirm"
  in data/README.md.
- Federal Reserve Bank of New York, Holston-Laubach-Williams estimates of the
  natural rate of interest, https://www.newyorkfed.org/research/policy/rstar.

Published studies cited in the parameter files and the documents (for example
Kilian, Iacoviello and Navarro, Gopinath and others) are cited for the values they
report; their text is not reproduced.

